  "//overrides": "Security patches for transitive deps flagged by `bun audit --prod --audit-level=high`. Pin to the fixed release; drop an entry once the direct parent ships it. brace-expansion GHSA-3jxr-9vmj-r5cp · postcss GHSA-6g55-p6wh-862q · fast-uri GHSA-4c8g-83qw-93j6. `sharp` is `$sharp` (npm-safe self-reference), NOT a version literal: sharp is ALSO a direct devDependency, and npm rejects (EOVERRIDE) overriding a direct dep to a differing spec — it broke the npm-based Lighthouse job. `$sharp` forces Next.js's transitive optional sharp (^0.34.5, < 0.35.0 libvips CVEs) up to the direct devDependency's version.",
